    "seo": {
      "title": "Citizen Service Systems in Iran | Iran, Unfolded",
      "description": "Understand Tehran's documented municipal feedback initiatives and why registering a request differs from verifying its resolution."
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "id": "documented-service-design",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "From receiving messages to following them through",
        "content": "A historical account published on Tehran council member Bahareh Arvin's website describes proposed improvements to the municipal systems known as 137 and 1888 within Tehran Man, the municipality's website and application. The account concerns a committee meeting in 2020; it is evidence of the work being discussed then, rather than a current service directory. [s1]\n\nThe proposals addressed registration, follow-up, and feedback. They also included publishing thematic maps and message information. Read together, these proposals reveal an important distinction in service design: receiving a resident's message is only one part of the process. Tracking how it is handled and reporting the result require additional functions. [s1]",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      },
      {
        "id": "plans-and-outcomes",
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "An improvement agenda is not proof of delivery",
        "content": "The meeting account proposed feedback during handling and at completion. It also discussed an application programming interface, a software connection intended to let other urban-service developers use registration and tracking functions. These were proposed actions, not demonstrated operating capabilities. The inspected account does not establish their completion, current availability, or effect on resolution times. [s1]\n\nA reliable contemporary guide therefore needs more than historical descriptions of digital features. This page remains a documented introduction pending verification of current channels, eligibility requirements, accessibility, and independently supported service outcomes.",
        "source_ids": ["s1"]
      }
    ],
